Overlay patch 0028: THE sibling-wide fuzzy-audio fix (2ship 0024 rev3,
device-confirmed 2026-07-19) — audio self-pump + producer guard + reservoir
+ audio-thread QoS + ring watermarks.

Root cause (confirmed shape in THIS port): GameEngine::HandleAudioThread is
the OLD coupled loop — a plain cv.wait() that produces audio only on the
game loop's per-tick notify. On iOS the game loop IS the UIKit main thread;
a pressed thumb's up-to-120 Hz touch events delay the notify past the
ring's headroom → backend drains → crackle. SoH upstream evolved this exact
loop (clicks fix #6594) which is why SoH alone is clean.

MANDATORY degeneracy check, done with THIS port's numbers: DesiredBuffered
= 1100 (Context Init {26800, 512, 1100}); one burst = NUM_AUDIO_CHANNELS(2)
× SAMPLES_HIGH(448) = 896 sample-frames. SoH's guard formula
(Buffered + burst <= Desired) would allow production only under 204
samples (~7.6 ms at 26.8 kHz) — the exact degeneration 2ship measured
(their 1680==burst). Using the rev2 intent form instead: produce while
Buffered <= Desired; overshoot bounded to one burst (~1996 ceiling).

Also: QOS_CLASS_USER_INTERACTIVE on the audio thread (2ship rev3 — calm-
window underruns under thermal pressure on default QoS), and min/max
buffered watermarks into atomics the 0014 rev4 probe reports as
aud_min/aud_max (0 = underrun; the retest instrument — coupled to 0014,
the series applies atomically). __IOS__-gated: the macOS build keeps
pristine upstream behavior. The 2S2H-style processing/cv_from_thread
handshake is preserved — the main thread's EndAudioFrame still waits for
processing==false per tick; notify only answers real gfx wakes.

